# The whole promise of this plugin is that every colleague's clone yields the same script engine.
# Leaving line endings to each machine's core.autocrlf would make that depend on local config, so
# pin them here. These are Windows PowerShell scripts driven by CSVs; CRLF is the correct target.
#
# Note: the original AM - PnPScript sources had MIXED endings (04/08/09 pure LF, 01 and MainScript
# part LF, the rest CRLF) from later edits. These rules normalize that to uniform CRLF. The script
# CONTENT is unchanged and PowerShell is indifferent to either ending — the point is determinism.

* text=auto

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.csv text eol=crlf

*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
